            },
            "body": "### Unrelated labels may bypass a failed performance gate\n\n**Medium Severity · Investigate**\n\nAfter a simulation PR fails the A/B measurement, adding any unrelated label starts another workflow run but skips this same `host tick A/B` job. GitHub treats skipped jobs as successful required checks, so if the newer same-name check supersedes the failed run, routine release/section labeling can unblock a performance regression without another measurement. Separate label handling from the required measurement check, or preserve the actual measurement result rather than emitting a successful skip. Verify GitHub's required-check selection for successive failed and skipped runs of this workflow on the same SHA.\n\n<!-- capy-badge:start -->\n<a href=\"https://capy.ai/pull/RayFernando1337/kongroyale/285\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://capy.ai/badge/neutral-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://capy.ai/badge/neutral-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Open in Capy\" src=\"https://capy.ai/badge/neutral-light.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- capy-badge:end -->",
